Nathan Fielder and Lance Oppenheim&#x2019;s &#x201C; You Can See Everything ,&#x201D; the Elizabeth Holmes documentary that became one of the year&#x2019;s most unlikely box office(and potential awards season) sensations, is now available to watch at home.

The A24 film arrived on digital platforms Tuesday morning, just over a month after its theatrical debut. It&#x2019;s available to purchase for $24.99 or rent for $19.99 on Prime Video and Apple TV. Related Stories Celebrity Streaming and Commerce Platform TalkShopLive Expands to TikTok Ahead of Black Friday Amazon Debuts $30 Streaming Bundle That Includes Starz, BritBox, AMC+, MGM+ and PBS Masterpiece In One Place

The digital release comes just days after &#x201C;You Can See Everything&#x201D; surpassed $100 million at the global box office , a staggering return for a nearly three-hour documentary that reportedly cost $7 million to produce. The film has grossed $93.5 million domestically, placing it among the highest-grossing documentaries in North American box office history. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The documentary picks up 34 days before Holmes, the disgraced founder of blood-testing startup Theranos, is set to report to federal prison following her conviction for defrauding investors. What begins as an intimate portrait of the former Silicon Valley darling evolves into a three-year filmmaking experiment that interrogates the relationship between documentary subjects and their filmmakers, and the slippery distinctions between performance and reality.

In his review of the film, Variety&#x2019;s Owen Gleiberman described it as &#x201C;a shameless, fascinating, reality-TV-eats-its-tale look at entitled duplicity&#x201D; and &#x201C;everything a great movie should be: an experience unlike one you&#x2019;ve had before, one that lures and enthralls you, and that leaves you feeling different when it&#x2019;s over.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

He also predicts that it could triumph at the Oscars because &#x201C;anyone who votes for it won&#x2019;t just be voting for best picture &#x2014; they&#x2019;ll be voting for the future.&#x201D;

David Fincher doesn't want to get tied up in big franchises anytime soon.

The &#x201C;Further Mis-Adventures of Cliff Booth&#x201D; director was interviewed on the Nov. 23 episode of Josh Horowitz&#x2019;s &#x201C;Happy Sad Confused&#x201D; podcast and spoke about his hesitancy about working on overly corporate projects.

&#x201C;I got offered &#x2026; what is the &#x2018; Lord of the Rings &#x2019; thing at Amazon?&#x201D; Fincher asked during the interview. Related Stories Amazon Debuts $30 Streaming Bundle That Includes Starz, BritBox, AMC+, MGM+ and PBS Masterpiece In One Place Celebrity Streaming and Commerce Platform TalkShopLive Expands to TikTok Ahead of Black Friday

&#x201C;Oh, 'Rings of Power,'&#x201D; Horowitz said. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;I got offered that &#x2026; to showrun,&#x201D; Fincher continued. &#x201C;This is before it went to Amazon, right? And I was like, &#x2018;No way.&#x2019; That is an extension of a corporate interest.&#x201D;

He pivoted to discussing how he didn't envy James Gunn and the position he accepted as co-CEO of DC Studios , which he recently announced he was leaving.

&#x201C;I mean, I look at James Gunn and I think, &#x2018;Those are bigger balls than I have. I would not &#x2026; take on DC and all of its dysfunction. Its innate DNA is dysfunctional.&#x2019;&#x201D;

&#x201C;I think there&#x2019;s a horrible constricting of the business right now,&#x201D; Fincher added later in the conversation. &#x201C;You know, with Paramount, Warner Bros. &#x2026; It&#x2019;s becoming more and more difficult to protect the individual voice in cinema.&#x201D;

Fincher also said that he once met with Kathleen Kennedy and had a long conversation with her about taking Lucusfilm public before it sold to Disney.

&#x201C;I was very interested in the idea of 'Star Wars' and what I said to her was, 'Why don&#x2019;t we go to Wall Street?'&#x201D; Fincher said.

&#x201C;Cliff Booth&#x201D; is opening on Imax screens on Nov. 25. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

